{
  "title": "57: al-Hadeed الحديد",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the name of Allah, the Beneficent, the Merciful.\nسَبَّحَ لِلَّهِ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَهُوَ الْعَزِيزُ الْحَكِيمُ (1)\nSABBAHA LELLAHE MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WA HOWA AL-A’AZEEZU AL-HAKEEMU.\nWhatever is in the heavens and the earth declares the glory of Allah, and He is the Mighty, the Wise.\nلَهُۥ مُلْكُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ يُحْىِۦ وَيُمِيتُ وَهُوَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيرٌ (2)\nLAHUL MULKUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE LAAHUL WAYUMEETU WA HOWA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEERUN.\nHis is the kingdom of the heavens and the earth; He gives life and causes death; and He has power over all things.\nهُوَ الْاَوَّلُ وَالْءَاخِرُ وَالظّٰهِرُ وَالْبَاطِنُ وَهُوَ بِكُلِّ شَىْءٍ عَلِيمٌ (3)\nHOWA AL-AAWLU WAL AAKHERU WAALZZAAHERU WAL BAATENU WA HOWA BEKULLE SHAYIN A’ALEEMUN.\nHe is the First and the Last and the Ascendant (over all) and the Knower of hidden things, and He is Cognizant of all things.\nهُوَ الَّذِى خَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ فِى سِتَّةِ اَيَّامٍ ثُمَّ اسْتَوَىٰ عَلَى الْعَرْشِ يَعْلَمُ مَا يَلِجُ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَمَا يَخْرُجُ مِنْهَا وَمَا يَنزِلُ مِنَ السَّمَآءِ وَمَا يَعْرُجُ فِيهَا وَهُوَ مَعَكُمْ اَيْنَ مَا كُنتُمْ وَاللَّهُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُونَ بَصِيرٌ (4)\nHOWA LAZIS KHALAQAL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA FIL SETTATE AYYAAMIN SUMMA ASTAWAA A’LAL A’RSHIL YA’LAMO MAA YALEJU FIL ARZE WA MAA YAKHROJO MINHAA WA MAA YANZELU MENAL SAMAAA-E WA MAA YAA’RUJU FEEHAA WA HOWA MA-A’KUM AYNA MAA KUNTUM WAALLLAHU BEMAA TAA’MALOONA BASEERUN.\nHe it is who created the heavens and the earth in six periods, and He is firm in power; He knows that which goes deep down into the earth and that which comes forth out of it, and that which comes down from the heaven and that which goes up into it, and He is with you wherever you are; and Allah sees what you do.\nلَّهُۥ مُلْكُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَاِلَى اللَّهِ تُرْجَعُ الْاُمُورُ (5)\nLLAHU MULKUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WA ELAL AL-LAHE TURJA-U’L AL-AUMOORU.\nHis is the kingdom of the heavens and the earth; and to Allah are (all) affairs returned.\nيُولِجُ الَّيْلَ فِى النَّهَارِ وَيُولِجُ النَّهَارَ فِى الَّيْلِ وَهُوَ عَلِيمٌۢ بِذَاتِ الصُّدُورِ (6)\nYOOLEJU LAYLA FIL AN-NAHAARE WAYOOLEJU NAHAARA FIL LAYLE WA HOWA A’ALEEMUN BE-ZAATIS AS-SUDOORE.\nHe causes the night to enter in upon the day, and causes the day to enter in upon the night, and He is Cognizant of what is in the hearts.\nءَامِنُوا۟ بِاللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِۦ وَاَنفِقُوا۟ مِمَّا جَعَلَكُم مُّسْتَخْلَفِينَ فِيهِ فَالَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ مِنكُمْ وَاَنفَقُوا۟ لَهُمْ اَجْرٌ كَبِيرٌ (7)\nAAMENOOA BEALLLAHE WARASOOLEHE WAANFEQOOA MIMMAA JAA’ALAKUM MMUSTAKHLAFEENA FEEHE FA LAZEENA AAMANOOA MENKUM WAANFAQOOA LAHUM AJRUN KABEERUN.\nBelieve in Allah and His Apostle, and spend out of what He has made you to be successors of; for those of you who believe and spend shall have a great reward.\nوَمَا لَكُمْ لَا تُؤْمِنُونَ بِاللَّهِ وَالرَّسُولُ يَدْعُوكُمْ لِتُؤْمِنُوا۟ بِرَبِّكُمْ وَقَدْ اَخَذَ مِيثٰقَكُمْ اِن كُنتُم مُّؤْمِنِينَ (8)\nWA MAA LAKUM LAA TUMENOONA BEALLLAHE WAALRRASOOLU YADU’OOKUM LETUMENOOA BE-RABBEKUM WA QAD AAKHAZA MEESAAQAKUM AEN KUNTUM MMUMENEENA.\nAnd what reason have you that you should not believe in Allah? And the Apostle calls on you that you may believe in your Lord, and indeed He has made a covenant with you if you are believers.\nهُوَ الَّذِى يُنَزِّلُ عَلَىٰ عَبْدِهِۦٓ ءَايٰتٍۭ بَيِّنٰتٍ لِّيُخْرِجَكُم مِّنَ الظُّلُمٰتِ اِلَى النُّورِ وَاِنَّ اللَّهَ بِكُمْ لَرَءُوفٌ رَّحِيمٌ (9)\nHOWA LAZIS YUNAZZELU A’LAA A’ABDEHEAA AAYAATIN BAYYENAAT LLEEKHREJAKUM MENAL ZOLOMAATE ELAL AN-NOORE WA INNA AL-LAHA BEKUM LARAOOFUN RRAHEEMUN.\nHe it is who sends down clear communications upon His servant, that he may bring you forth from utter darkness into light; and most surely Allah is Kind, Merciful to you.\nوَمَا لَكُمْ اَلَّا تُنفِقُوا۟ فِى سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ وَلِلَّهِ مِيرٰثُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ لَا يَسْتَوِى مِنكُم مَّنْ اَنفَقَ مِن قَبْلِ الْفَتْحِ وَقٰتَلَ اُو۟لٰٓئِكَ اَعْظَمُ دَرَجَةً مِّنَ الَّذِينَ اَنفَقُوا۟ مِنۢ بَعْدُ وَقٰتَلُوا۟ وَكُلًّا وَعَدَ اللَّهُ الْحُسْنَىٰ وَاللَّهُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُونَ خَبِيرٌ (10)\nWA MAA LAKUM ALLAA TUNFEQOOA FIL SABEELE AL-LAHE WALELLAHE MEERAASU SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE LAA YASTAWEAA MENKUM MAN AANFAQA MEN QABLE AL-FATHE WAQAATALA OOLAAA-EKA AAA’ZAMU DARAJATAN MENAL LAZEENA AANFAQOOA MEN BA’DO WAQAATALOOA WAKULLAN WA-A’DAR AL-LAHU AL-HUSNAA WAALLLAHU BEMAA TAA’MALOONA KHABEERUN.\nAnd what reason have you that you should not spend in Allah's way? And Allah's is the inheritance of the heavens and the earth, not alike among you are those who spent before the victory and fought (and those who did not): they are more exalted in rank than those who spent and fought afterwards; and Allah has promised good to all; and Allah is Aware of what you do.\nمَّن ذَا الَّذِى يُقْرِضُ اللَّهَ قَرْضًا حَسَنًا فَيُضٰعِفَهُۥ لَهُۥ وَلَهُۥٓ اَجْرٌ كَرِيمٌ (11)\nMMAN ZAL LAZIS YUQREZUL AL-LAHA QARZAN HASANAN FAYUZAAE’EFAHU LAHUL WALAHUAA AJRUN KAREEMUN.\nWho is there that will offer to Allah a good gift so He will double it for him, and he shall have an excellent reward.\nيَوْمَ تَرَى الْمُؤْمِنِينَ وَالْمُؤْمِنٰتِ يَسْعَىٰ نُورُهُم بَيْنَ اَيْدِيهِمْ وَبِاَيْمٰنِهِم بُشْرَىٰكُمُ الْيَوْمَ جَنّٰتٌ تَجْرِى مِن تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ خٰلِدِينَ فِيهَا ذٰلِكَ هُوَ الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِيمُ (12)\nYAWMA TARAL AL-MUMENEENA WAL-MOAMENAATE YASA’AA NOORUHUM BAYNA AAYDEEHEM WABEAAYMAANEHEM BUSHRAAKUMU YAWMA LAHUM TAJREAA MEN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA ZAALEKA HOWA FAWZUL AL-A’AZEEMU.\nOn that day you will see the faithful men and the faithful women-- their light running before them and on their right hand-- good news for you today: gardens beneath which rivers flow, to abide therein, that is the grand achievement.\nيَوْمَ يَقُولُ الْمُنٰفِقُونَ وَالْمُنٰفِقٰتُ لِلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ انظُرُونَا نَقْتَبِسْ مِن نُّورِكُمْ قِيلَ ارْجِعُوا۟ وَرَآءَكُمْ فَالْتَمِسُوا۟ نُورًا فَضُرِبَ بَيْنَهُم بِسُورٍ لَّهُۥ بَابٌۢ بَاطِنُهُۥ فِيهِ الرَّحْمَةُ وَظٰهِرُهُۥ مِن قِبَلِهِ الْعَذَابُ (13)\nYAWMA YAQOOLU AL-MUNAAFEQOONA WAL MUNAAFEQAATU LELLAZEENA AAMANOOA ANZUROONAA NAQTABES MEN NNOOREKUM QEELA ARJEU’OOA WARAAAKUM FAL TAMESOOA NOORAN FAZUREBA BAYNAHUM BESOORIN LLAHU BAABUN BAATENUHU FEEHE AR-RAHMATU WAZAAHERUHU MEN QEBALEHE A’ZAABO.\nOn the day when the hypocritical men and the hypocritical women will say to those who believe: Wait for us, that we may have light from your light; it shall be said: Turn back and seek a light. Then separation would be brought about between them, with a wall having a door in it; (as for) the inside of it, there shall be mercy in it, and (as for) the outside of it, before it there shall be punishment.\nيُنَادُونَهُمْ اَلَمْ نَكُن مَّعَكُمْ قَالُوا۟ بَلَىٰ وَلٰكِنَّكُمْ فَتَنتُمْ اَنفُسَكُمْ وَتَرَبَّصْتُمْ وَارْتَبْتُمْ وَغَرَّتْكُمُ الْاَمَانِىُّ حَتَّىٰ جَآءَ اَمْرُ اللَّهِ وَغَرَّكُم بِاللَّهِ الْغَرُورُ (14)\nYUNAADOONAHUM ALAM NAKUN MMAA’AKUM QAALUD BALAA LAA-KINNAKUM FATANTUM AANFUSAKUM WATARABBASTUM WA TABTUM WAGHARRATKUMU AL-AAMAANEAAAU HATTAA JAAA-A AMRUL AL-LAHE WAGHARRAKUM BEALLLAHE AL-GHAROORU.\nThey will cry out to them: Were we not with you? They shall say: Yea! but you caused yourselves to fall into temptation, and you waited and doubted, and vain desires deceived you till the threatened punishment of Allah came, while the archdeceiver deceived you about Allah.\nفَالْيَوْمَ لَا يُؤْخَذُ مِنكُمْ فِدْيَةٌ وَلَا مِنَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ مَاْوَىٰكُمُ النَّارُ هِىَ مَوْلَىٰكُمْ وَبِئْسَ الْمَصِيرُ (15)\nFALYAWMA LAA YOAKHAZO MENKUM FIDYATUN WA LAA MENAL LAZEENA KAFARUL MAAWAAKUMU TAMASSANAN HEYA MAWLAAKUM WA BEASAL AL-MASEERU.\nSo today ransom shall not be accepted from you nor from those who disbelieved; your abode is the fire; it is your friend and evil is the resort.\nاَلَمْ يَاْنِ لِلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓا۟ اَن تَخْشَعَ قُلُوبُهُمْ لِذِكْرِ اللَّهِ وَمَا نَزَلَ مِنَ الْحَقِّ وَلَا يَكُونُوا۟ كَالَّذِينَ اُوتُوا۟ الْكِتٰبَ مِن قَبْلُ فَطَالَ عَلَيْهِمُ الْاَمَدُ فَقَسَتْ قُلُوبُهُمْ وَكَثِيرٌ مِّنْهُمْ فٰسِقُونَ (16)\nALAM YAANE LELLAZEENA AAMANOOA AAN TAKHSHAA’A QULOOBUHUM LE-ELAA AL-LAHE WA MAA NAZALA MENAL HAQQE WA LAA YAKOONOOA KA-LAZEENA AOOTOOA KETAABA MEN QABLO FATAALA A’LAYHEMUL AL-AAMADU FA QASAT QULOOBUHUM WAKASEERUN MINHUM FAASEQOONA.\nHas not the time yet come for those who believe that their hearts should be humble for the remembrance of Allah and what has come down of the truth? And that they should not be like those who were given the Book before, but the time became prolonged to them, so their hearts hardened, and most of them are transgressors.\nاعْلَمُوٓا۟ اَنَّ اللَّهَ يُحْىِ الْاَرْضَ بَعْدَ مَوْتِهَا قَدْ بَيَّنَّا لَكُمُ الْءَايٰتِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَعْقِلُونَ (17)\nAA’LAMOOA ANNAL AL-LAHA LAAHUL ARZA BA’DA MAWTEHAA QAD BAYYANNAL LAKOMUL AL-AAYAATE LA-A’LLAKUM TAA’QELOONA.\nKnow that Allah gives life to the earth after its death; indeed, We have made the communications clear to you that you may understand.\nاِنَّ الْمُصَّدِّقِينَ وَالْمُصَّدِّقٰتِ وَاَقْرَضُوا۟ اللَّهَ قَرْضًا حَسَنًا يُضٰعَفُ لَهُمْ وَلَهُمْ اَجْرٌ كَرِيمٌ (18)\nINNAL AL-MUSSADDEQEENA WAL MUSSADDEQAATE WAAQRAZOOA AL-LAHA QARZAN HASANAN YUZAAA’AFU LAHUM WA LAHUM AJRUN KAREEMUN.\nSurely (as for) the charitable men and the charitable women and (those who) set apart for Allah a goodly portion, it shall be doubled for them and they shall have a noble reward.\nوَالَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ بِاللَّهِ وَرُسُلِهِۦٓ اُو۟لٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الصِّدِّيقُونَ وَالشُّهَدَآءُ عِندَ رَبِّهِمْ لَهُمْ اَجْرُهُمْ وَنُورُهُمْ وَالَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ وَكَذَّبُوا۟ بَِٔايٰتِنَآ اُو۟لٰٓئِكَ اَصْحٰبُ الْجَحِيمِ (19)\nWA LAZEENA AAMANOOA BEALLLAHE WARUSULEHEAA OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL AS-SEDDEEQOONA WA EZAA E’ENDA RABBEHIM LAHUM AJROHUM WANOORUHUM WA LAZEENA KAFARUL WAKAZZABOOA BEAYAATENAA OOLAAA-EKA ASHAABUN AL-JAHEEME.\nAnd (as for) those who believe in Allah and His apostles, these it is that are the truthful and the faithful ones in the sight of their Lord: they shall have their reward and their light, and (as for) those who disbelieve and reject Our communications, these are the inmates of the hell.\nاعْلَمُوٓا۟ اَنَّمَا الْحَيَوٰةُ الدُّنْيَا لَعِبٌ وَلَهْوٌ وَزِينَةٌ وَتَفَاخُرٌۢ بَيْنَكُمْ وَتَكَاثُرٌ فِى الْاَمْوٰلِ وَالْاَوْلٰدِ كَمَثَلِ غَيْثٍ اَعْجَبَ الْكُفَّارَ نَبَاتُهُۥ ثُمَّ يَهِيجُ فَتَرَىٰهُ مُصْفَرًّا ثُمَّ يَكُونُ حُطٰمًا وَفِى الْءَاخِرَةِ عَذَابٌ شَدِيدٌ وَمَغْفِرَةٌ مِّنَ اللَّهِ وَرِضْوٰنٌ وَمَا الْحَيَوٰةُ الدُّنْيَآ اِلَّا مَتٰعُ الْغُرُورِ (20)\nAA’LAMOOA ANNAMAA AL-HAYAWTU DUNYAA LAE’EBUN WA LAHWUNW WAZEENATUN WATAFAAKHURUN BAYNAKUM WATAKAASURUN FIL AL-AAMWAALE WAL AAWLAADE KAMASALIL GHAYSIN AAA’JABA KUFFAARA NABAATUHU SUMMA YAHEEJU FATARAAHU MUSFARRAL SUMMA YAKOONU HUTAAMAN WA AL-AAKHERATE A’ZAABUN SHADEEDUN WAMAGHFERATUN MENAL AL-LAHE WAREZWAANUN WA MAA AL-HAYAWTU AD-DUNYAA ILLAA MATAAU’U AL-GHUROORE.\nKnow that this world's life is only sport and play and gaiety and boasting among yourselves, and a vying in the multiplication of wealth and children, like the rain, whose causing the vegetation to grow, pleases the husbandmen, then it withers away so that you will see it become yellow, then it becomes dried up and broken down; and in the hereafter is a severe chastisement and (also) forgiveness from Allah and (His) pleasure; and this world's life is naught but means of deception.\nسَابِقُوٓا۟ اِلَىٰ مَغْفِرَةٍ مِّن رَّبِّكُمْ وَجَنَّةٍ عَرْضُهَا كَعَرْضِ السَّمَآءِ وَالْاَرْضِ اُعِدَّتْ لِلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ بِاللَّهِ وَرُسُلِهِۦ ذٰلِكَ فَضْلُ اللَّهِ يُؤْتِيهِ مَن يَشَآءُ وَاللَّهُ ذُو الْفَضْلِ الْعَظِيمِ (21)\nSAABEQOOA AELAA MAGHFERATIN MMEN RABBEKUM WA JANNATIM A’ARZUHAA KAA’ARZE SAMAAA-E WAL ARZE O-I’DDAT LELLAZEENA AAMANOOA BEALLLAHE WARUSULEHE ZAALEKA FAZLUL AL-LAHE YUTEEHE MAN YASHAAA WAALLLAHU ZUL FAZLIL AL-A’AZEEME.\nHasten to forgiveness from your Lord and to a garden the extensiveness of which is as the extensiveness of the heaven and the earth; it is prepared for those who believe in Allah and His apostles; that is the grace of Allah: He gives it to whom He pleases, and Allah is the Lord of mighty grace.\nمَآ اَصَابَ مِن مُّصِيبَةٍ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَلَا فِىٓ اَنفُسِكُمْ اِلَّا فِى كِتٰبٍ مِّن قَبْلِ اَن نَّبْرَاَهَآ اِنَّ ذٰلِكَ عَلَى اللَّهِ يَسِيرٌ (22)\nMAA ASAABA MEN MMUSEEBATIN FIL ARZE WA LAA FEAAAA AANFUSEKUM ILLAA FIL KETAABIM MMEN QABLE AAN NNABRAAHAA INNAL ZAALEKA A’LAL AL-LAHE YASEERUN.\nNo evil befalls on the earth nor in your own souls, but it is in a book before We bring it into existence; surely that is easy to Allah:\nلِّكَيْلَا تَاْسَوْا۟ عَلَىٰ مَا فَاتَكُمْ وَلَا تَفْرَحُوا۟ بِمَآ ءَاتَىٰكُمْ وَاللَّهُ لَا يُحِبُّ كُلَّ مُخْتَالٍ فَخُورٍ (23)\nLLEKAYLAA TAASAWA A’LAA MAA FAATAKUM WA LAA TAFRAHOOA BEMAA AATAAKUM WAALLLAHU LAA YOHIBBUL KULLA MUKHTAALIN FAKHOORIN.\nSo that you may not grieve for what has escaped you, nor be exultant at what He has given you; and Allah does not love any arrogant boaster:\nالَّذِينَ يَبْخَلُونَ وَيَاْمُرُونَ النَّاسَ بِالْبُخْلِ وَمَن يَتَوَلَّ فَاِنَّ اللَّهَ هُوَ الْغَنِىُّ الْحَمِيدُ (24)\nLAZEENA YABKHALOONA WAYAAMUROONA NAASA BIL-BUKHLE WAMAN YATAWALLA FA-INNAL AL-LAHA HOWA AL-GHANEAAAU AL-HAMEEDU.\nThose who are niggardly and enjoin niggardliness on men; and whoever turns back, then surely Allah is He Who is the Selfsufficient, the Praised.\nلَقَدْ اَرْسَلْنَا رُسُلَنَا بِالْبَيِّنٰتِ وَاَنزَلْنَا مَعَهُمُ الْكِتٰبَ وَالْمِيزَانَ لِيَقُومَ النَّاسُ بِالْقِسْطِ وَاَنزَلْنَا الْحَدِيدَ فِيهِ بَاْسٌ شَدِيدٌ وَمَنٰفِعُ لِلنَّاسِ وَلِيَعْلَمَ اللَّهُ مَن يَنصُرُهُۥ وَرُسُلَهُۥ بِالْغَيْبِ اِنَّ اللَّهَ قَوِىٌّ عَزِيزٌ (25)\nLAQAD ARSALNAA RUSULANAA BIL-BAYYENAATE WAANZALNAA MA-A’HOMUL KETAABA WAL MEEZAANA LEEQOOMA NAASO BIL QISTE WAANZALNAA AL-HADEEDA FEEHE BAASUN SHADEEDUN WAMANAAFEU’U LIN-NAASE WALEEA’LAMA AL-LAHU MAN YANSURUHU WARUSULAHU BIL-GHAYBE INNAL AL-LAHA QAWEAAAUN A’AZEEZUN.\nCertainly We sent Our apostles with clear arguments, and sent down with them the Book and the balance that men may conduct themselves with equity; and We have made the iron, wherein is great violence and advantages to men, and that Allah may know who helps Him and His apostles in the secret; surely Allah is Strong, Mighty.\nوَلَقَدْ اَرْسَلْنَا نُوحًا وَاِبْرٰهِيمَ وَجَعَلْنَا فِى ذُرِّيَّتِهِمَا النُّبُوَّةَ وَالْكِتٰبَ فَمِنْهُم مُّهْتَدٍ وَكَثِيرٌ مِّنْهُمْ فٰسِقُونَ (26)\nWA LAQAD ARSALNAA NOOHAN WAABRAAHEEMA WA JA-A’LNAA FIL ZURREETEHEMAA NOBUWWATA WAL KETAABA FAMENHUM MMUHTADIN WAKASEERUN MINHUM FAASEQOONA.\nAnd certainly We sent Nuh and Ibrahim and We gave to their offspring the (gift of) prophecy and the Book; so there are among them those who go aright, and most of them are transgressors.\nثُمَّ قَفَّيْنَا عَلَىٰٓ ءَاثٰرِهِم بِرُسُلِنَا وَقَفَّيْنَا بِعِيسَى ابْنِ مَرْيَمَ وَءَاتَيْنٰهُ الْاِنجِيلَ وَجَعَلْنَا فِى قُلُوبِ الَّذِينَ اتَّبَعُوهُ رَاْفَةً وَرَحْمَةً وَرَهْبَانِيَّةً ابْتَدَعُوهَا مَا كَتَبْنٰهَا عَلَيْهِمْ اِلَّا ابْتِغَآءَ رِضْوٰنِ اللَّهِ فَمَا رَعَوْهَا حَقَّ رِعَايَتِهَا فََٔاتَيْنَا الَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ مِنْهُمْ اَجْرَهُمْ وَكَثِيرٌ مِّنْهُمْ فٰسِقُونَ (27)\nSUMMA QAFFAYNAA A’ALAA AASAAREHEM BERUSULENAA WA QAFFAYNAA BEE’EESAA MARYAM MARYAMAL WAAATAYNAAHU AL-AENJEELA WA JA-A’LNAA FIL QULOOBE LAZEENA ATTABAU’OOHU RAAFATAN WA RAHMATAM WARAHBAANEETAN ABTADAU’OOHAA MAA KATABNAAHAA A’LAYHIM ILLAA TEGHAAA-A REZWAANE AL-LAHE FAMAA RAA’AWHAA HAQQA REA’AAYATEHAA FAATAYNAA LAZEENA AAMANOOA MINHUM AJRAHUM WAKASEERUN MINHUM FAASEQOONA.\nThen We made Our apostles to follow in their footsteps, and We sent Isa son of Marium afterwards, and We gave him the Injeel, and We put in the hearts of those who followed him kindness and mercy; and (as for) monkery, they innovated it-- We did not prescribe it to them-- only to seek Allah's pleasure, but they did not observe it with its due observance; so We gave to those of them who believed their reward, and most of them are transgressors.\nيٰٓاَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ اتَّقُوا۟ اللَّهَ وَءَامِنُوا۟ بِرَسُولِهِۦ يُؤْتِكُمْ كِفْلَيْنِ مِن رَّحْمَتِهِۦ وَيَجْعَل لَّكُمْ نُورًا تَمْشُونَ بِهِۦ وَيَغْفِرْ لَكُمْ وَاللَّهُ غَفُورٌ رَّحِيمٌ (28)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOOA TAQUL AL-LAHA WAAAMENOOA BERASOOLEHE YUTEKUM KEFLAYNE MEN RRAHMATEHE WAYAJA’AL LAKUM NOORAN TAMSHOONA BEHIL WA YAGHFIR LAKUM WAALLLAHU GHAFOORUN RRAHEEMUN.\nO you who believe! be careful of (your duty to) Allah and believe in His Apostle: He will give you two portions of His mercy, and make for you a light with which you will walk, and forgive you, and Allah is Forgiving, Merciful;\nلِّئَلَّا يَعْلَمَ اَهْلُ الْكِتٰبِ اَلَّا يَقْدِرُونَ عَلَىٰ شَىْءٍ مِّن فَضْلِ اللَّهِ وَاَنَّ الْفَضْلَ بِيَدِ اللَّهِ يُؤْتِيهِ مَن يَشَآءُ وَاللَّهُ ذُو الْفَضْلِ الْعَظِيمِ (29)\nLLEALLAA YAA’LAMA AAHLU KETAABE ALLAA YAQDEROONA A’LAA SHAY-IN MMEN FAZLIL AL-LAHE WA ANNAL FAZLA BEEDE AL-LAHE YUTEEHE MAN YASHAAA WAALLLAHU ZUL FAZLIL AL-A’AZEEME.\nSo that the followers of the Book may know that they do not control aught of the grace of Allah, and that grace is in Allah's hand, He gives it to whom He pleases; and Allah is the Lord of mighty grace.",
  "merits": "This is a ‘Madani’ Surah and it has 29 verses. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said that the reciter of this Surah will be counted from among the staunch believers. Imam Muhammad al-Baqir (a.s.) has said that whoever recites all the Surahs that start with Tasbih of Allah (s.w.t.) before going to sleep, will not die before meeting the 12th Holy Imam (a.s.) and after his death, he will have the honour of being a neighbour of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.).\nIt is narrated from Imam Ja’far as-Sadiq (a.s.) that if Surah al-Hadeed and al-Mujaadelah are recited in the compulsory prayers frequently, then the reciter will never face any punishment of Allah (s.w.t.) in this world and will not see any evil from his family. If recited by a prisoner, he will be released soon. If worn on the neck as a talisman, the wearer will not be killed in war. This Surah also makes one courageous."
